{"book":{"id":"book-redefining-rape-sexual-violence-in-the-era-of-suffrage-and-segregation-estelle-b-freedman","slug":"redefining-rape-sexual-violence-in-the-era-of-suffrage-and-segregation-estelle-b-freedman","title":"Redefining Rape: Sexual Violence in the Era of Suffrage and Segregation","authors":[{"id":"person-estelle-b-freedman","name":"Estelle B. Freedman"}],"publisherId":"publisher-harvard-university-press","imprintId":"imprint-harvard-university-press","isbn13":["9780674724846"],"subjects":["Race & Ethnicity"],"topics":["Civil Rights & Racial Justice","Black History & Culture","Crime, Policing & Violence","Gender & Feminism"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Redefining%20Rape%3A%20Sexual%20Violence%20in%20the%20Era%20of%20Suffrage%20and%20Segregation%20Estelle%20B.%20Freedman","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Redefining%20Rape%3A%20Sexual%20Violence%20in%20the%20Era%20of%20Suffrage%20and%20Segregation%20Estelle%20B.%20Freedman","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Redefining%20Rape%3A%20Sexual%20Violence%20in%20the%20Era%20of%20Suffrage%20and%20Segregation%20Estelle%20B.%20Freedman","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Redefining%20Rape%3A%20Sexual%20Violence%20in%20the%20Era%20of%20Suffrage%20and%20Segregation%20Estelle%20B.%20Freedman","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/books/OL25997643M"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-oah-darlene-clark-hine-award-oah-darlene-clark-hine-award-official-page-internet-archive-snapsho","source-open-library-redefining-rape-sexual-violence-in-the-era-of-suffrage-and-segregation-estelle-b-freedman","source-imprint-normalization"],"publicationYear":2013,"pageCount":387,"summary":"\"Rape has never had a universally accepted definition, and the uproar over \"legitimate rape\" during the 2012 U.S. elections confirms that it remains a word in flux. Redefining Rape tells the story of the forces that have shaped the meaning of sexual violence in the United States, through the experiences of accusers, assailants, and advocates for change. In this ambitious new history, Estelle Freedman demonstrates that our definition of rape has depended heavily on dynamics of political power and social privilege.The long-dominant view of rape in America envisioned a brutal attack on a chaste white woman by a male stranger, usually an African American. From the early nineteenth century, advocates for women's rights and racial justice challenged this narrow definition and the sexual and political power of white men that it sustained.","thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/7533828-L.jpg","displaySummary":"In this ambitious new history, Estelle Freedman demonstrates that our definition of rape has depended heavily on dynamics of political power and social privilege.The long-dominant view of rape in America envisioned a brutal attack on a chaste white woman by a male stranger, usually an African American. From the early nineteenth century, advocates for women's rights and racial justice challenged this narrow definition and the sexual and political power of white men that it sustained.","primarySubject":"Race & Ethnicity","primaryTopic":"Civil Rights & Racial Justice","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Race & Ethnicity","confidence":"low","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Race & Ethnicity","score":5,"evidenceCount":3},{"subject":"American History","score":4,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Gender & Sexuality","score":3,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"True Crime & Justice","score":3,"evidenceCount":2},{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":2,"evidenceCount":1},{"subject":"History","score":1,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"award_category","rawLabel":"American History","mappedSubject":"American History","score":2,"confidence":"low","sourceId":"source-award-record-oah-darlene-clark-hine-award-oah-darlene-clark-hine-award-official-page-internet-archive-snapsho","id":"subject-evidence-book-redef